 "notes": "Observed 95% CL upper limits on g_agamma from Fig. 3 (figures/adbc_gagg_bounds2.pdf), the paper's headline result. Five 300-kHz datasets over 9.88-10.45, 11.92-12.22 and 13.12-13.69 MHz (40.9-43.3, 49.3-50.6, 54.4-56.7 neV); gaps between bands are unprobed. Vector paths (blue strokes) extracted with pymupdf; x calibrated on the MHz axis ticks (reproduces stated band edges to <0.01 MHz), y on the log gridlines 1e-10..1e-6 GeV^-1. The plotted limit is a noisy Feldman-Cousins curve (~1000 vertices per dataset); reported points are per-bin medians (15 bins per dataset, 75 points). Overall median 1.7e-8 GeV^-1 vs paper's quoted average sensitivity 1.9e-8 GeV^-1. Mass = h*f with h = 4.1357e-15 eV/Hz. Assumed local DM density 0.3 GeV/cm^3.",
